 type\\|General\" venue.md venue-artifacts.json README.md | head -20; cat venue-artifacts.json | head -40", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/repo; git pull -q; grep -n -i \"contribution type\\|General\" venue.md venue-artifacts.json README.md | head -20; cat venue-artifacts.json | head -40"]], "output": "```console\nvenue.md:75:- **Contribution type (chosen by the authors, cannot be changed after submission, reviewers judge by it):** General (default; \"most submissions\"), Theory, Use-inspired, Concept & Feasibility, Negative Results (https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines; form field `contribution_type`). **Negative Results** has \"a high\" significance and originality bar: the result must be \"grounded in deeper analysis\", \"informative in changing how the community addresses a question\", and \"surprising or unexpected in some way\"; \"not simply an empirical observation that some experiment did not turn out as expected\". **For `story-repo`:** a study whose headline may be \"the source matrix gives little / nothing beats stratified sampling\" should be framed as a **General** paper whose claims are the controlled comparison, the bias–variance accounting and the ceiling analysis (an evaluation paper), and only claim the Negative Results type if the analysis supplies the grounded explanation (the outline's C2 and C4 are that grounding). The objective itself values well-supported negative results.\n{\"artifact_schema\":1,\"required_paper_files\":[\"paper/main.tex\",\"paper/references.bib\",\"paper/template/neurips_2026.sty\",\"paper/template/checklist.tex\",\"code/\"]}\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "f39dc66b-8738-5c7e-8ca9-4a5dffe65057", "at": 1795671355.986794, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14427, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "b4fdb2546f2f17abc0138791dffb3da2", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label